### Timeline Extended: vanilla's three HUD visibility templates
### (game/gui/block_windows.gui:984-1000, vanilla 1.14.5), redefined so the
### HUD hides under the Timeline Extended window's Full Screen as it does under
### vanilla's full-screen panels: the outliner, the wars list, the lens
### toolbar and the notifications beside the outliner (half_and_fullscreen_hide),
### the "Paused" frame, the construction box and the backgrounds of the time
### controls and the top bar (fullscreen_hide), and the compact notifications
### in their place (half_and_fullscreen_show). The Side Panel keeps the HUD.
###
### WHY A 00_ FILE. A template's name is global, and the engine keeps the
### first definition it reads, in file-name order across vanilla and the mods,
### and logs each later one in gui.log as "Template 'X' already registered at
### '<file>'" (gotcha #30 in docs/guides/gui_modding_guide.md). This name
### sorts before block_windows.gui, so these win and vanilla's whole file stays
### vanilla's.
###
### EACH TEMPLATE is vanilla's expression, its Or chain verbatim, ORed with two
### more terms (one line each, as vanilla writes them):
###   - the Community Mod Framework's full-screen key, com_fullscreen. CMF
###     (Workshop 3385002128) redefines these three in 00_com_fullscreen_hide.gui
###     with that key added; whichever file loads first wins, so with this term
###     CMF's full screens keep hiding the HUD if this one does. Nothing sets
###     the key without CMF.
###   - the Timeline Extended window's Full Screen: the window root's visible
###     AND the full-screen frame's (gui/te_systems_window.gui), so the HUD
###     hides exactly while the frame draws. Every route that closes the window
###     clears com_open_window, so the HUD comes back by each, though
###     te_systems_window_wide is remembered for the session.
### Vanilla leaves the treaty draft out of fullscreen_hide, a half-screen
### panel that keeps the time controls; the window's Full Screen covers the
### screen as the Politics panel does, so it is in all three.
###
### test_te_fullscreen_hud.py holds each to vanilla's (the fixture
### test_fixtures/vanilla_gui/block_windows.gui) plus these two terms, the
### window's term to the root and the frame, And and Or to two arguments each.
### A vanilla patch that changes the three: change them here.

### If the widget should NOT be visible in fullscreens, not taking the Treaty Draft panel into account.
template fullscreen_hide {
	visible = "[Not( Or( Or( Or(Or(Or(Or(InformationPanelBar.IsPanelOpen('politics'), InformationPanelBar.IsPanelOpen('politics_panel_change_law')), InformationPanelBar.IsPanelOpen('tech_tree')), InformationPanelBar.IsPanelOpen('pop_browser')), InformationPanelBar.IsPanelOpen('building_browser')), GetVariableSystem.Exists('com_fullscreen') ), And( And( And( GetMetaPlayer.GetPlayedOrObservedCountry.IsValid, Not( GetMetaPlayer.IsObserver ) ), GetVariableSystem.HasValue('com_open_window', 'te_systems_window') ), GetVariableSystem.Exists('te_systems_window_wide') ) ) )]"
}

### If the widget should be visible when ANY fullscreen is open, including the Treaty Draft panel.
template half_and_fullscreen_show {
	visible = "[Or( Or( Or(Or(Or(Or(Or(InformationPanelBar.IsPanelOpen('politics'), InformationPanelBar.IsPanelOpen('politics_panel_change_law')), InformationPanelBar.IsPanelOpen('tech_tree')), InformationPanelBar.IsPanelOpen('pop_browser')), InformationPanelBar.IsPanelOpen('building_browser')), InformationPanelBar.IsPanelOpen('treaty_draft_panel')), GetVariableSystem.Exists('com_fullscreen') ), And( And( And( GetMetaPlayer.GetPlayedOrObservedCountry.IsValid, Not( GetMetaPlayer.IsObserver ) ), GetVariableSystem.HasValue('com_open_window', 'te_systems_window') ), GetVariableSystem.Exists('te_systems_window_wide') ) )]"
}

### If the widget should NOT be visible when ANY fullscreen is open, including the Treaty Draft panel.
template half_and_fullscreen_hide {
	visible = "[Not( Or( Or( Or(Or(Or(Or(Or(InformationPanelBar.IsPanelOpen('politics'), InformationPanelBar.IsPanelOpen('politics_panel_change_law')), InformationPanelBar.IsPanelOpen('tech_tree')), InformationPanelBar.IsPanelOpen('pop_browser')), InformationPanelBar.IsPanelOpen('building_browser')), InformationPanelBar.IsPanelOpen('treaty_draft_panel')), GetVariableSystem.Exists('com_fullscreen') ), And( And( And( GetMetaPlayer.GetPlayedOrObservedCountry.IsValid, Not( GetMetaPlayer.IsObserver ) ), GetVariableSystem.HasValue('com_open_window', 'te_systems_window') ), GetVariableSystem.Exists('te_systems_window_wide') ) ) )]"
}
